.nh
.TH "PB-INBOX-PATH" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-inbox-path - Show this machine's Inbox directory


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb inbox path [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Print the directory on this machine where received files are written. It is a setting of
this machine only and has nothing to do with where your own sends go.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for path

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print JSON


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  pb inbox path
  pb inbox path --json
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-inbox(1)\fP
